IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sec49-nouns`
IMPORT `sec49-cross-references`

-- Row il-49. The sound citation points at what its citing words say, the two amending instructions say what the page images show, and the recorded facts about the two defects are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their four failing assertions are in sec49-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in sec49-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- Control B: section 56(ב) lists section 38, which stands; the citing words and the target are described alike.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 38, a section on a court order`)
-- The target of the control is not a repealed section.
#ASSERT (NOT ((`reference: s 56(ב) to s 38, a section on a court order`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a section of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text`))
-- Control A1: Amendment 50 section 27(1) conforms the Fifth Schedule item (3)(א); control A2: section 28 changes Part B item (7) of the Seventh Schedule and does not delete the words.
#ASSERT `the instruction conforms its schedule item to the repeal` (`instruction: Amendment 50 s 27(1), Fifth Schedule item (3)(א)`)
#ASSERT (NOT `the instruction conforms its schedule item to the repeal` (`instruction: Amendment 50 s 28, Seventh Schedule Part B item (7)`))
#ASSERT (`instruction: Amendment 50 s 27(1), Fifth Schedule item (3)(א)`)'s `the schedule and item it changes` EQUALS "Fifth Schedule, item (3), paragraph (א)"
#ASSERT (`instruction: Amendment 50 s 28, Seventh Schedule Part B item (7)`)'s `the schedule and item it changes` EQUALS "Seventh Schedule, Part B, item (7)"
#ASSERT (`instruction: Amendment 50 s 27(1), Fifth Schedule item (3)(א)`)'s `the instruction was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`instruction: Amendment 50 s 28, Seventh Schedule Part B item (7)`)'s `the instruction was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- No citation here has both limbs read from the official instruments alone: each has a limb that is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY, either the whole limb or what follows the page read.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 38, a section on a court order`))
-- Defect A: limb (a), the repeal and its commencement, from the page images with the caveat; limb (b), the words as enacted, from the page image with the wider caveat.
#ASSERT (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the same words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official page image of the words as enacted; where those words stand and that no later instrument touched them are CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- Defect B: limb (a) as above; limb (b), the words of section 56(ב), is the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the same words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
-- Control B: the same two kinds as defect B.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 38, a section on a court order`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the same words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 38, a section on a court order`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`

§ `Tests of what the two descriptions of the defects say`

-- What the citing words say it points at, and what the target is, as the texts show them.
#ASSERT (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `paragraph (2) of subsection (ב) of section 35ד of the Law, whose wording this row did not read`
#ASSERT (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a section of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `section 14א of the Law, whose wording this row did not read`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a section of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text`

§ `Tests of the day the named text stopped being in force`

-- Defect A. Section 7 of Amendment 50 repeals section 35ד; section 29(א) commences the Law three months after publication on 8 August 2012. The row types 9 November 2012, the first day certain on either counting (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`) (Date 9 11 2012) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`) (Date 10 11 2012) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day before and the earlier days: the row does not say (8 November 2012 is the other possible commencement day; 8 August 2012 is the day of publication; 27 January 2011 is the day the words were enacted).
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`) (Date 8 11 2012) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`) (Date 8 8 2012) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: Seventh Schedule Part C item (2) to s 35ד(ב)(2)`) (Date 27 1 2011) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Defect B. Section 9(1) of Sefer HaChukim 2253 repeals section 14א; section 13 commences the Law on 8 Tevet 5771 = 15 December 2010.
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`) (Date 15 12 2010) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`) (Date 16 12 2010) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day before and the day of publication: the row does not say (fork F5 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`) (Date 14 12 2010) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 14א`) (Date 27 7 2010) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A control has no recorded end: NOTHING on any day, which is not a statement that the target stands.
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: s 56(ב) to s 38, a section on a court order`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
